1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
KANB AI Agropreneur: an AI plant doctor for Malaysian farmers.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:15,000
We did not train our own model. We tested a general AI model on 75,000+ labelled photos from public datasets, improved the app around it, and re-tested.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The farmer takes a photo. The app checks that it is clear enough.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The farmer chooses the crop, here padi.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
A saved tomato scan: the app names the likely disease, how sure it is, and asks an expert to review when unsure.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
When unsure, it names the look-alike diseases and what to check for each.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Diseased plants get KANB plant-health products, clearly marked as support, not a cure.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:55,000
What testing found, and what we changed.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
With the chosen model, the right disease is in the top three for 76% of the same photos, up from 49%. Padi 96%, chilli 71%.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The more accurate model is more confident when wrong. A second AI check is built for this, and is being measured next.

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
A KANB product now appears on 98 of 100 scans, up from 23.
